# Data conversion between kilobyte and terabyte

Verifies direct data conversion between kilobyte and terabyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1KB to 0.0000TB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5KB yields 0.0000TB; backward, converting 1TB to 1000000000KB preserves the integer representation across the integer coarser-to-finer scale, while 1.5TB yields 1500000000.0KB. Tiny magnitudes round to four fractional digits.

>>> source
const forward_whole: int = 1KB
print(forward_whole->to(TB))
const forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5KB
print(forward_fractional->to(TB))
const backward_whole: int = 1TB
print(backward_whole->to(KB))
const backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5TB
print(backward_fractional->to(KB))

<<< stdout
0.0000TB
0.0000TB
1000000000KB
1500000000.0KB

<<< stderr
